Summary Report: “AWS Cloud and AI Day Hanoi - Watch Party Ho Chi Minh City” Event Objectives Explore the latest AWS technology trends centered on Agentic AI, data analytics, and application modernization. Hear practical perspectives from technology leaders, government representatives, and leading Vietnamese enterprises on digital transformation. Experience live AI solution demos and connect with the Cloud/AI community at the AWS Vietnam office (Bitexco Financial Tower, Ho Chi Minh City). Shape an engineering mindset around applying Agentic Systems to software development workflows and cloud infrastructure optimization. Speakers H.E. Hoàng Minh – Deputy Minister of Science and Technology H.E. Jennifer Wicks – U.S. Ambassador to Vietnam Dr. Werner Vogels – CTO, Amazon.com Eric Yeo – Country General Manager, Malaysia, Vietnam &amp; Indochina, AWS Dr. Jens Lottner – Chief Executive Officer, Techcombank Mai Lê – Director of Product Management, Katalon Key Highlights Strategic Direction from the Opening Keynote Core theme: &ldquo;What if we asked ourselves, &lsquo;Why not make every idea possible?&rsquo;&rdquo;
Explored how AWS equips builders with tools to push creative boundaries and bring ideas to production on the cloud. Highlighted the shift toward Agentic AI: autonomous agent systems capable of decomposing tasks, invoking APIs, and executing multi-step workflows. Enterprise lessons from digital banking (Techcombank) and automated software testing (Katalon) on adopting Cloud and Generative AI to improve customer experience. Modern Data &amp; Application Architecture Trends Modern Data &amp; Analytics: Optimizing Data Lakes on Amazon S3, reducing heavy ETL bottlenecks, and unifying analytics pipelines to power AI models. Microservices &amp; Serverless Evolution: Combining virtual machines, container clusters (ECS/EKS), and Serverless (AWS Lambda) thoughtfully to balance cost and deployment speed. Enterprise-scale Security: Centralized identity governance, end-to-end encryption, and financial-grade cloud security practices. Technology Showcase (Expo &amp; Community Zones) 8-Bit Agents Activation: Hands-on zone for building, configuring, and deploying AI Agents to solve automated challenges within minutes. Startup Zone: Showcased real-world Fintech, AI, and commerce solutions built by local startups on AWS. Developer Community Zone: Direct networking with AWS Solutions Architects and the AWS User Group Vietnam community. Key Takeaways Design Mindset Agent-First Mindset: AI is evolving beyond simple text copilots into autonomous agents that interact directly with backend APIs and databases. Data-centric Architecture: Clean, well-structured data forms the essential foundation for reliable AI applications and analytics systems. Continuous Modernization: Digital transformation is an ongoing process that favors loosely-coupled architectures for scalability. Technical Architecture Integrating Generative AI (Amazon Bedrock) and Machine Learning (Amazon SageMaker) into existing data pipelines. Pairing Event-Driven Architecture with AI agents to trigger automated business workflows when events occur. Choosing compute infrastructure pragmatically between containers and serverless based on latency and workload profiles. Adoption Strategy Taking a phased modernization approach, starting by organizing and cleaning the data layer before adding intelligent automation features. Evaluating return on investment (ROI) alongside new technology adoption to avoid unnecessary cloud spend. Applying to Work Experimenting with AI Agents: Explore building prototype AI agents on Amazon Bedrock to automate data queries and repetitive engineering tasks. Optimizing Data Pipelines: Apply S3 Data Lake concepts combined with Amazon Athena querying for analytics coursework and lab projects. Applying AWS Security Best Practices: Enforce Least Privilege with IAM and monitor system behavior through CloudWatch. Event Experience Attending AWS Cloud and AI Day Hanoi - Watch Party Ho Chi Minh City at the AWS Vietnam office (Bitexco Financial Tower, Floors 26 &amp; 36) on September 29, 2026 was a particularly valuable learning and networking experience:
Learning from top industry leaders Following keynote talks from Amazon CTO Dr. Werner Vogels and executive leaders gave me a broader perspective on global-scale distributed architecture. Enterprise case studies from Techcombank&rsquo;s CEO and Katalon&rsquo;s Director of Product Management illustrated practical Cloud and AI adoption in strict production environments. Hands-on technical and product exposure Visiting the Expo zone and trying the 8-Bit Agents Activation clarified how an AI Agent progresses from prompt input to autonomous tool execution. Observed how local tech startups turn product ideas into commercial deployments using AWS cloud services. Community networking and engagement Well-organized check-in and badge pickup on the 26th floor combined with a smooth livestream connection to the Hanoi main stage. Direct conversations with AWS Solutions Architects and engineers in the Ho Chi Minh City tech community clarified real-world skill expectations. Lessons learned The rise of Agentic AI requires engineers to build cleaner APIs and structured data layers that AI agents can interact with reliably, rather than relying solely on isolated prompts. The spirit of &ldquo;Why not make every idea possible?&rdquo; encourages taking initiative with cloud tools to prototype software ideas rapidly and safely. Some event photos Overall, the event not only kept me up to date with AWS&rsquo;s latest cloud and AI advances, but also inspired me and gave me a clearer direction for growing my career in Cloud Computing and Artificial Intelligence.
